#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553626} :activity/id #uuid "9bf1e7a1-3d42-5972-990b-72f857972080" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050502 :topic/id #uuid "4e4e9d7a-bee2-5790-9304-d063d47d2ed1" :topic/math-academy-id 3640} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f92ae5e-4722-51a3-8719-8262bf80d2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552997} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7381ca-a062-5633-8a25-41b8653790e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553031} {:answer/id #uuid "61c27318-4129-5567-b96e-c20827c015ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553078} {:answer/id #uuid "e59a9fd1-8ffe-5eaa-b0a0-e71a9df33db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553325} {:answer/id #uuid "e61f81f7-40e3-5ace-8c33-5fb7063d84f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553326} :answer-field/id #uuid "b648352b-9cfb-5d5c-8ea0-b1cb8e46e03c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca240843-51e6-5695-9d1f-64a8db44b027" :question/math-academy-id "q-143663" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}{y}^{2}, & 2\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x<1,\\,-4<y<1.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $x<1,\\,-4<y<1,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](images/0c/0c027a6d656653ee1158bdff681405afe99748d734555f515de563099146849e.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=∅.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo there is nowhere in our region $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={∬}_{Δ}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "191a9709-ec5c-5263-bac1-283c8d8f7000" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553663}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553626 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10cfccf1-6913-579b-9563-ad8ececa56bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552893} {:answer/id #uuid "26bb8339-8625-5c2e-be3d-633afe38be4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552937} {:answer/id #uuid "37725566-96f7-5f90-9538-94991485d005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552977} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d2e28f-fffc-5482-b340-aeff1f21fab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553225} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2fc514-21f7-5325-94ab-cf2fd0236392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553306}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552893} :answer-field/id #uuid "29f3fcfe-72a9-5dde-8a8a-0d962e42b063" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7e8f43e3-d7f0-593f-9f61-7957ca2c311e" :question/math-academy-id "q-143659" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}, & -1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x<-1,\\,y>2.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1,\\,y>2,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](images/04/04eee4bcf3263318946503732ed7715913e12949659cacb84e93d1696ee7f2e1.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=∅.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo there is nowhere in our region $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={∬}_{Δ}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "69db2255-e176-5209-8d02-619b8b9048bd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553603}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553628 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e1edfbb-97a6-5512-b70a-6e8d8202000f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553039} {:answer/id #uuid "56c8630f-1621-5e8d-809b-4d2c5ad8b94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553054} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb7531a-12d9-526b-85d6-9ee848e15e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553065} {:answer/id #uuid "8707bc17-722e-5ad2-b68e-45d04cefeabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553140} {:answer/id #uuid "b19432ec-9898-5227-bca5-d283658bf48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553224}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553224} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3273a24-dde6-50e8-9d77-b0d57e06622e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "392c7844-059b-541a-9161-f7e9d9b52570" :question/math-academy-id "q-143708" :question/problem "Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x,y),$ where\n\n$$\nF(8,6)=0.8,\\,F(8,2)=0.5,\\,F(2,6)=0.4,\\,F(2,2)=0.2.\n$$\n\nFind $P(2\\le X\\le 8,2\\le Y\\le 6).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $F(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)$ is the probability that the pair $(X,Y)$ will lie inside the infinite rectangular region that has its top-right corner at $(x,y)$ and whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axes.\n\nLet's sketch the region corresponding to the probability we wish to find.\n\n![](images/15/1524afeeaea3cc0fd4ee51b9572222bdd846fba378e029e4fa20a272a4fe6353.png)\n\nGeometrically, this region can be obtained as follows:\n\n1\\. Take the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(8,6).$\n\n2\\. Subtract the infinite rectangles that have their top-right corners at $(8,2)$ and $(2,6).$\n\n3\\. Finally, we need to *add back* the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(2,2).$ This is because we subtracted this region twice in step 2.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 8,2\\le Y\\le 6) & =\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(8,6)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 8,Y\\le 6)}} \\\\  & \\,-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(8,2)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 8,Y\\le 2)}}-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(2,6)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 2,Y\\le 6)}} \\\\  & \\,+\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(2,2)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 2,Y\\le 2)}} \\\\  & =F(8,6)-F(8,2)-F(2,6)+F(2,2) \\\\  & =0.8-0.5-0.4+0.2 \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6b1b9c05-8e73-5803-a166-04d6b3142c0b"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553663 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553530 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aeb199f-b948-5795-9348-3e5e109c2652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552948} {:answer/id #uuid "42dfda97-5990-5386-9a3e-eab1d6c81981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553007} {:answer/id #uuid "436a0b26-8a41-555d-8ec3-92df6c6037dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553008} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb7ea56-a736-5085-98e7-33c9b2e06200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553036} {:answer/id #uuid "7302919e-aae8-52d6-be57-1c5a122ace53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553104}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553104} :answer-field/id #uuid "2184ddd6-bb84-56f9-ac10-b6a376a8e0a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "64924153-c273-5495-a9b7-e1268d0994d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-143696" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y, & 1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](images/00/00e0dcbd7ea22f09db76b03fc4d7bda328f1b1f17ceeb998cf039241dafd8da3.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le x,\\,0\\le v\\le y\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{4}u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v{\\int }_{1}^{x}u\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v{[\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}]}_{u=1}^{u=x}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{2}-1){\\int }_{0}^{y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{2}-1)[\\operatorname{sin}⁡v]_{v=0}^{v=y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b2ed5b00-2fd7-55f9-9dbf-26e347814268" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553628}}] :activity/title "The Joint CDF of Two Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552859}]}
